.Dd September 19, 2026
.Dt ADDUSER 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm adduser
.Nd create an account
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Ss os-simple
.Nm
.Op Fl u Ar UID
.Op Fl s Ar SHELL
.Ar NAME
.Ss os-real
.Nm
.Op Ar OPTIONS
.Ar USER
.Op Ar GROUP
.Sh DESCRIPTION
On os-simple,
.Nm
creates an account using this project's account databases.
The caller's real user ID must be 0.
The program is not set-id and refuses other callers before opening any file.
.Pp
Unless
.Fl u
is given, the program chooses the lowest number from 1000 through 60000
that is unused as both a user ID and a group ID.
The login shell defaults to
.Pa /bin/sh ;
its existence is not checked.
.Pp
One credential transaction protects the account checks, number selection,
and four publications, in this order:
.Bl -enum -compact
.It
A shadow entry with the locked password field
.Ql \&! .
.It
A group entry.
.It
A home directory with mode 0700.
.It
A passwd entry.
.El
.Pp
This order prevents an interruption from leaving a visible account
without a locked shadow record.
After releasing the credential lock,
.Nm
runs
.Ql passwd NAME .
The account remains locked until its password is set.
A failure reports the entries already published and does not remove them.
.Pp
On os-real,
.Nm
is the BusyBox applet.
It creates
.Ar USER ,
or adds an existing
.Ar USER
to
.Ar GROUP .
Its options differ from those of the os-simple program.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Ss os-simple
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl u Ar UID
Use this number for the user and group IDs.
It must be unused in both databases.
.It Fl s Ar SHELL
Use this login shell instead of
.Pa /bin/sh .
.El
.Ss os-real
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h Ar DIR
Use this home directory.
.It Fl g Ar GECOS
Set the GECOS field.
.It Fl s Ar SHELL
Use this login shell.
.It Fl G Ar GRP
Use this group.
.It Fl S
Create a system user.
.It Fl D
Do not assign a password.
.It Fl H
Do not create a home directory.
.It Fl u Ar UID
Use this user ID.
.It Fl k Ar SKEL
Use this skeleton directory instead of
.Pa /etc/skel .
.El
.Sh FILES
The os-simple program updates:
.Bl -tag -width /home/NAME
.It Pa /etc/shadow
Locked password entry.
.It Pa /etc/group
Group entry.
.It Pa /home/NAME
Home directory.
.It Pa /etc/passwd
Account entry.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
As root, run:
.Dl adduser alice
Then answer the password prompts.
.Ql tests/run account
exercises account creation on both images.
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
The following diagnostics are from the os-simple program.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ql adduser: only root may create an account
The caller's real user ID is not 0.
.It Ql adduser: NAME already exists
The name occurs in all three account databases.
.It Ql adduser: NAME is in FILES but not FILE; remove the leftover lines and retry
The name occurs in only some of the databases.
The message identifies them; the program neither resumes nor removes
the partial account.
.It Ql adduser: failed after writing FILES; nothing was rolled back
A failure occurred after one or more publications.
The message lists the published files and, if created, the home directory.
.It Ql adduser: /etc/shadow was not written; nothing was changed
The first publication failed.
.It Ql adduser: what was written is live but may not survive a power cut
A published credential file could not be flushed.
No further account entries are published.
.It Ql adduser: NAME exists; the transaction did not end cleanly
The account was published, but releasing the credential transaction failed.
.It Ql adduser: NAME exists and cannot be entered; run passwd NAME
The account was published, but the password program could not be executed.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr passwd 1 ,
.Xr passwd 5 ,
.Xr busybox-loginutils 8
